{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[('peer_response_admission','internal/raft/peer.go',184,197),('response_classification','internal/raft/entryutils.go',103,112),('received_message_dispatch','node.go',1274,1316),('candidate_vote_admission','internal/raft/raft.go',2029,2046),('vote_deduplication','internal/raft/raft.go',1076,1094),('vote_request_producer','internal/raft/raft.go',1096,1131),('membership_remove','internal/raft/raft.go',1196,1225),('member_kinds','internal/raft/raft.go',374,427)]\nsources=[dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind='code_observation') for i,f,a,b in rows]\nids=[x['id'] for x in sources]+['term_admission','authority_reset']\ns=dict(action='explained',rationale='Dispose of the specific apparent missing sender-membership guard in handleVoteResp by following the actual network consumer. Do not extrapolate to accumulated votes across a concurrent membership transition.',sources=sources,question=dict(question='Can a RequestVoteResp whose sender is absent from the current voting membership reach the candidate vote tally through the normal received-message path merely because handleVoteResp itself checks only duplicate identity?',source_ids=ids,disposition='explained_by_existing_mechanism',preferred_check='source_review',importance='Counting an unqualified response could form election authority without the applicable voting quorum.',counterevidence=['node.handleReceivedMessages routes RequestVoteResp through Peer.Handle; handleMessage has no special vote-response bypass.','Peer.Handle classifies RequestVoteResp as a response and only forwards it when the sender is in remotes, observers or witnesses. A sender absent from all three is dropped before term processing or tallying.','A known observer passes Peer.Handle but is rejected by handleCandidateRequestVoteResp before handleVoteResp. Witnesses are voting members under votingMembers and numVotingMembers.','removeNode deletes the sender from all three maps, so a later-delivered response from that removed sender is rejected at the outer boundary.','For admitted senders, term handling excludes lower-term responses, reset clears old votes on term change, and handleVoteResp deduplicates by sender.'],unknowns=[],trigger_rationale='The local tally has no membership test, but the sourced outer dispatcher and observer guard supply it. This is a local admission answer for a response delivered after membership exclusion, not an answer about support already accumulated before membership changed.'),feedback=dict(ref_ids=['peer_response_admission','candidate_vote_admission','b4f1a4d97742470b8148df31692f8215'],answered='The vote-admission suspicion is explained by the actual normal dispatch chain. Also corrected a source locator limitation: earlier peer_admission (peer.go 195-211) included only the tail of Handle and GetUpdate, not its membership predicate. New peer_response_admission (184-197) supplies the full predicate previously inspected. The ReadIndex finding itself depends on read_confirmation, read_batch and the actual ReadyToRead endpoint, and its all-known-member history is unchanged by this citation correction.',remaining=['Investigate whether asynchronous application/configuration handoff can let election or read-support state outlive its applicable membership context.','Witness availability assumptions and recovery paths remain only partially examined.'],rationale='Read actual vote producer, caller, response classifier, guard, tally and membership deletion. No constructed vote response or execution is needed to establish this branch-local exclusion. Retain the source-range correction explicitly without rerunning the unaffected context-preservation witness.'))\nPath('vote_admission_explained.json').write_text(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-10_13-34-50-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission vote_admission_explained.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
